{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And when the sun grew hot, it melted.</b> What remained in the field became streams, and gazelles and deer drink from them, and the nations of the world hunt them and taste in them the taste of manna, and they know how praiseworthy Israel is." "<b>And it melted.</b> פָּשַׁר — a term of פּוֹשְׁרִים: by means of the sun it warms and thaws; דישטנ״פריר בְּלַעַז. And its parallel is in Sanhedrin at the end of the four deaths."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French destempre/détrempier, 'to dissolve, thaw'; Rashi refers to the last Mishnah of Sanhedrin chapter 7 (the four modes of execution)."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:43.186118236Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}